transcript.content:
Archived projects no longer count toward the active badge, even when their `active` field is true.

- **The fix:** a one-line change in `src/domain/Active_Count.ts`. `selectActiveCount` now counts a project only if it is active and not archived.
- **New tests:** `src/domain/Active_Count.test.ts` checks four cases:
  - active projects that aren't archived are counted;
  - archived projects are never counted, whether or not they're active;
  - inactive projects are ignored;
  - an empty list gives zero.
- **Checks:** `npm run gate` (lint, typecheck, tests) passes, with 6 of 6 tests passing. I also ran the new tests against the old code: the "archived but active" test failed there, so it does catch this bug.

I didn't touch any existing test file, `package.json`, the build config or the check scripts. I haven't committed anything.
